 "note": "M, 17 platforms, mirrored both ways. Two gears mesh in the middle and share one stone, the gearbox (C). Each gear's rim is a speed lane that turns: the left gear clockwise, the right one anticlockwise (on both, the top runs toward the middle and the bottom away from it). Two drives turn both gears: the crown stones over and under the gearbox (X and Y) are linked speed relays - fire EITHER and both gears turn the other way (hold one drive and you can flip the gears even if the other side holds the other). The gearbox is a ROTOR on its two diagonals: one joins top-left to bottom-right, the other bottom-left to top-right; with the gears turning as they start, the first is the left player's fast lane through the middle and the second the right player's (firing the drive swaps that). The long dry ways round are the arches over the top (by the drive) and under the bottom. Each home has three ways onto its gear: the straight road to its point and a curved road to its top and bottom corners. Finale: the figure-eight round the gearbox - both gears' inner corners and hubs.",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "experimental": false,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "R07": "Daniele 2026-11-05: the bottom drive Y is linked to the top drive X (one shared state, the same rim lanes), so it drives no deck of its own; X's R07 margin is Y's - ACCEPTED by Daniele 2026-11-06 (Desk)"
 },
